In article <8631@attctc.DALLAS.TX.US>, fres@attctc.DALLAS.TX.US (Brian Long) writes:
> In article <20287@cup.portal.com> FelineGrace@cup.portal.com (Dana B Bourgeois) writes:
> >Also, how about adding stairs that end in pits?  or some other nasty trap? 
> >in the middle of a group of monsters?  I think that will allow players to die
> >over a shorter period of time than if you just had random stairs. 
 
What fun is "allowing players to die over a shorter period of time"?
I would think the goal of Nethack 3.0 is to make the game more CHALLENGING,
not just HARDER.  Getting into sticky situations would be fine, but let's
not go overboard and create staircases which descend into spiked pits full
of acid and amphibious black dragons...

> Hey that inspires a new Idea!  How about around level 10 there are stair cases
> that lead to levels that are not really in the maze, say like level A-Z.. 
> They get you no further in the game, and when you exit the level you are 
> back on the level you were last on, You could have fake staircases leading
> down to these levels that appear around level 10.  These levels would be REAL
> hard, a struggle to get out of!  What do you think?

Now THIS is more interesting.  Have a fake staircase which looks like
an ordinary one (except maybe if you zap it with cancellation or something)
which leads to an alternate plane.  This is a level in which the only way
out is to kill a particular monster.  When you kill that monster you get
back where you started, and the magic staircase is gone (or becomes a plain
staircase).  These magic levels could have particular motifs, i.e. an Alice
in Wonderland level, a Frost Giant level, etc.  Woe to the brave knight who's
expecting to escape a danger, forgets to Cancel the down-staircase, and finds
himself on the Killer Bees from Hell level...

